## Michael's Memo: The Advisor Who Refused to Walk Away

Every business owner knows the feeling. Payroll due, cash tied up, and the clock ticking.

And everyone who advises a business knows the other side of that call. You want to help. But the credit box in front of you says no.

That's the moment that defines an advisor's reputation. This month's story is about a banker who refused to walk away from it.

When a Florida wedding venue faced a critical cash shortfall during its busiest month, their banker didn't say, "Sorry, we can't help." He said, "I know someone who can."

Within three business days, Serve Funding helped deliver exactly what the client needed: $150,000 in working capital to keep fifteen weddings, booked over three consecutive weeks, on schedule, with staff paid and operations thriving.

The result wasn't just a funded deal. It was a relationship saved, and an advisor remembered as the one who showed up when it mattered most.

We exist to help create more moments like that.

Here to serve,

Michael Kodinsky, Founder & CEO

## Deal Highlight: $150K in Three Days

When the owner of a Florida wedding venue realized they couldn't cover payroll ahead of a packed schedule of fifteen weddings in three weeks, panic set in. Their banker recognized the urgency and made the introduction.

Together, we reviewed competing offers and identified better, fairer terms, educated the client on repayment options and prepay discounts, and delivered $150K in 72 hours: fast, affordable, and transparent.

The full story is in the case study: [Proactive Banker Saved a Venue's Wedding Season](/blog/banker-saved-wedding-season).

## Creative Capital Solution: Flexible Funding for Situational Opportunities

When a business hits a cash flow wall during its busiest season, the fix has to be fast and it has to be fair.

**Product snapshot:**

- Funding amounts: $25K to $500K
- Speed to close: 2 to 5 business days
- Terms: 12 to 24 months
- Lien position: subordinate to any bank or SBA credit facility
- Use case: payroll, vendor payables, inventory, or seasonal prep

**Why it works:** it sits behind an existing bank relationship rather than disturbing it, it moves at the speed the moment demands, and it turns "we can't help" into "here's who can."

## More Than Money: Core Value of the Month, Responsibility

At Serve Funding, responsibility means more than delivering capital. It means protecting the trust that already exists around a business.

- We take personal ownership of the client's needs from the first call to the last payment.
- We make sure whoever brought us in is credited for it, from start to finish.
- We never cross-sell or compete for the relationships a business already has.

When we're introduced to a business, that business stays exactly whose it was, and the credibility of everyone involved grows with every successful outcome.
